WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.144
After Shu Han fell, the last ruler Liu Shan was brought to Luoyang and moved into a luxurious big house arranged by the Jin court.

00:00:09.494 --> 00:00:16.502
One day, Sima Zhao held a banquet for him and deliberately arranged a song-and-dance performance from Shu.

00:00:16.852 --> 00:00:21.316
The musicians began to play, and the dancers danced gracefully.

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:28.890
The former Shu officials present all wept sadly; only Liu Shan watched happily, even clapping and cheering.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:36.200
Someone deliberately asked him: do you miss Shu? Smiling, Liu Shan shook his head.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.942
Sima Zhao listened carefully to his answer from the side.

00:00:41.292 --> 00:00:49.164
He answered: I am so happy here, I do not miss Shu at all.

00:00:49.514 --> 00:00:54.458
Hearing this, Sima Zhao laughed loudly, thinking he had no ambition at all.

00:00:54.808 --> 00:01:02.992
From then on, 'so happy he did not miss Shu' became a famous expression, describing people who only care about pleasure and forget their roots.

